   10)Diff. between HashMap and TreeMap? Are they thread safe?
The primary function of TreeMap is to maintain order. It helps us in the storage of keys in a sorted manner in ascending order. The HashMap does not function to maintain any order. The primary function of the LinkedHashMap is to maintain an order in which we would insert the key-value pairs.
HashMap implements Map interface while TreeMap implements SortedMap interface. A Sorted Map interface is a child of Map. HashMap implements Hashing, while TreeMap implements Red-Black Tree(a Self Balancing Binary Search Tree).
HashMap implements Map interface while TreeMap implements SortedMap interface. A Sorted Map interface is a child of Map. HashMap implements Hashing, while TreeMap implements Red-Black Tree(a Self Balancing Binary Search Tree).
TreeMap does not allow duplicate keys,
TreeMap does allow null keys. but allows null values. 
Thread safety is not inherent to TreeMap
The HashMap is unordered .
Why HashMap is not thread-safe?
The reason is that the HashMap object referenced by the static variable cache is shared by all calls to isPrime() , and HashMap is not threadsafe. If multiple threads mutate the map at the same time, by calling cache. 
